cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this course or the code, please cite it as below."
title: "Snake RL from scratch: reinforcement-learning theory, hands-on code and a browser demo"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Kartik"
    family-names: "Anagawadi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kartik-A-1820/snake-rl-from-scratch"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A free reinforcement-learning course built on one small game: tabular Q-learning, DQN and its upgrades,
  and PPO, with interactive notes, bit-identical JavaScript and Python engines, GPU-batched environments,
  multi-seed ablations and trained agents that play in the browser.
keywords: [reinforcement learning, DQN, PPO, Snake, education, PyTorch]
